- `src/ui.rs:301` leaves `selected_agent` and the active chat window pointing at an agent after `set_agent_hidden_state(..., true)` hides it. `src/terminal_app.rs:846` uses this path when a completed feature is closed, so after the user answers `yes` in `src/workspace.rs:265` the left pane hides that row but the right pane can still be the closed agent's chat. With multiple agents, `clamp_control_selection()` can make the left selection point at a different visible row while typed chat still routes to the hidden `selected_agent` through `src/terminal_app.rs:679`. The existing manual hide path in `src/ui.rs:937` explicitly handles this by reselecting the visible control row when the hidden agent was selected; the new programmatic hide path needs the same state repair or a deliberate closed-chat surface.

